-- Kids games handbook -> curriculum_weeks.kids_game (52 weeks, one game each).
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Signal in the Static — Everyone hums, chatters and shuffles — that''s the noise. One child hides a beeping timer or shaker somewhere in the hall. The room has to go quiet enough, in stages, to hear it and find it. Repeat with the noise starting louder each time.' WHERE week_number = 1;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Label Tag — Each child wears a sticky label on their back with a made-up word (Sparkly, Slow, Loud, Bossy). Others treat them as that label for two minutes. Then everyone guesses their own label, peels it off and says one true thing about themselves instead.' WHERE week_number = 2;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Freeze in the Gap — Music plays and everyone moves. When it stops, freeze — but before you freeze you must take one big breath. Facilitator calls a feeling (''cross!'', ''excited!'') and children move like that, then freeze and breathe again.' WHERE week_number = 3;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Body Weather Report — Children move around. Facilitator calls a scenario (''you''re about to do a speech'', ''you''re getting a present''). Everyone freezes and puts a hand where they feel it — tummy, chest, head, hands. Then a quick show of hands: who felt it in the tummy?' WHERE week_number = 4;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Kind Mirror — Pairs face each other. One moves slowly, the other mirrors. Swap. Then each says one true, kind thing they noticed about their partner — how they moved, how carefully they copied.' WHERE week_number = 5;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Same Cup — Each child gets an identical cup with a different amount of water. They compare, complain, negotiate — then discover that pouring into one big jug fills it exactly the same either way.' WHERE week_number = 6;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Boo Ball / Cheer Ball — Two soft balls. The ''boo ball'' is passed while the room says something grumpy and unhelpful (''you''ll never do it''). The ''cheer ball'' is passed with something honest and kind. Pass them at the same time and notice which one people want.' WHERE week_number = 7;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Iceberg Hunt — Big feelings are written on cones at one end (ANGRY, GRUMPY, SHOUTY). Underneath each, hidden in a beanbag pile, are the small feelings (worried, left out, tired, hungry). Teams race to find what''s underneath their big feeling.' WHERE week_number = 8;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Safe Hands Relay — Children carry something fragile — an egg, a full cup, a tower of blocks — across the hall and hand it to a named safe grown-up at the other end. The point of the game is the handover, not the speed.' WHERE week_number = 9;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Mask Off — Each child holds a paper plate with a big smile drawn on it in front of their face and answers ''how are you?'' from behind it. Then they lower it and answer again. No one has to say anything different — but they can.' WHERE week_number = 10;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Backpack Game — Volunteers wear a backpack loaded with soft objects, each one labelled with something invisible (''didn''t sleep'', ''lost my lunch'', ''moved house''). They try to do a simple task — hop, catch, skip. The room guesses what might be in the bag.' WHERE week_number = 11;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Loop Track — Chalk or tape a loop on the floor with three stations: TRIGGER, WHAT I DO, WHAT I GET. Children walk their own loop for a habit (bored → tablet → fun) and then try walking a different second station.' WHERE week_number = 12;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Treasure Map Review — Thirteen stations around the hall, one per week, each with a picture from that session. Children move around collecting a stamp and saying one thing they remember. Ends with the whole map on the wall.' WHERE week_number = 13;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Red Light, Own Light — Standard red light / green light, but after three rounds the facilitator stops calling. Children have to decide themselves when to move. Some freeze waiting. Talk about waiting for permission that isn''t coming.' WHERE week_number = 14;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Costume Swap — A pile of dress-ups. Children are told to dress as what other people expect them to be, walk the hall, then swap into what they''d actually pick. Two laps, two feelings.' WHERE week_number = 15;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Heavy Beanbags — Each grudge is a beanbag. Children name something they''re cross about (or make one up) and add a beanbag to their arms. Then they try to catch, hug or high-five while holding them all. They can put one down whenever they like.' WHERE week_number = 16;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Do-Over Station — Skittles or a bean-bag toss. Everyone misses on purpose first. Then everyone gets a do-over and a friendly line to say to themselves: ''that''s okay, go again.'' Nobody keeps score.' WHERE week_number = 17;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Coach in Your Ear — One child does a simple challenge (balance on a line, bounce a ball ten times). One partner plays the mean voice quietly, one plays the honest kind coach. Swap. Which one helped?' WHERE week_number = 18;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Yes/No Islands — Two hoops: YES and NO. Facilitator calls out things (''want to be first?'', ''want a hug from someone you don''t know?'', ''want to share your snack?''). Children jump to their honest answer. No one is allowed to comment on anyone else''s island.' WHERE week_number = 19;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Never-Ending Cheer — One child is cheered by the room. Then two. Then everyone at once. The room notices that the cheering did not run out — unlike a bag of sweets, which is passed around alongside it and does.' WHERE week_number = 20;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Follow the Leader Chain — A leader starts a movement, the line copies. Every 30 seconds the leader goes to the back and a new one starts. At the end: which move did you keep doing even after that leader was gone?' WHERE week_number = 21;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Fortress — Children build a wall around themselves from soft blocks or cushions, then try to pass a ball to a friend through it. Then they take one block out. Then another. How much wall do you actually need?' WHERE week_number = 22;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Autumn Leaves — Everyone holds a paper leaf with something that ended written or drawn on it. On a signal they let them fall. Then the leaves are swept into a pile and seeds or paper flowers are planted in it.' WHERE week_number = 23;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Burnt Toast Alarm — A loud alarm goes off at random. Children freeze, then check: is it a fire, or is it burnt toast? A card is revealed each time — most say burnt toast. They practise the check before reacting.' WHERE week_number = 24;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Old Coat — Children put on a coat several sizes too small (or a tiny hat) and try to move. It fitted once. Then they swap for one that fits now.' WHERE week_number = 25;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Backpack Empty-Out — Children carry a heavy-ish backpack around a course. Then they name one thing to take out, remove a weight, and do the course again. And again. Notice the difference each time.' WHERE week_number = 26;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Build-a-Me Statue — In pairs, one child sculpts the other into a statue of ''who I want to be'' — brave, calm, kind. Photograph nothing; just walk the gallery and guess. Then everyone strikes their own chosen pose at once.' WHERE week_number = 27;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Rescue the Treasures — Ten objects scattered in the hall, a rope ''river'' across the middle. Teams may only carry three across. They must decide together which three matter most, and say why.' WHERE week_number = 28;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'One Brick at a Time — Every child adds one block to a shared tower each time they complete a small action — ten star jumps, one kind word, tying a lace. Fast building is not allowed. One brick, one action.' WHERE week_number = 29;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Foundation Wobble — Teams build the tallest tower they can on a wobbly base (a cushion). Then rebuild on a firm one. Same blocks, different base.' WHERE week_number = 30;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Garden Circle — Children plant themselves as ''seeds'' around the hall. Some spots are near the music and cheering, some near a grumpy corner. Everyone tries to grow (stretch up) in their spot. Then they choose a new one.' WHERE week_number = 31;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Echo Hall — One child says something to the far wall; the room echoes it back. Say something harsh — the room echoes it harshly. Say something kind — same. The room only gives back what was sent.' WHERE week_number = 32;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Rhythm Course — An obstacle course is run in a random order first — chaotic, tiring. Then it''s run in a set rhythm with a drumbeat. Same course, different feeling.' WHERE week_number = 33;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Rest Station — A relay where every third lap you must lie down on a mat for 30 seconds. Teams that skip the rest get slower. Teams that rest properly get faster.' WHERE week_number = 34;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Junk Orchestra — A pile of random objects. In small groups, children have five minutes to make an instrument and a sound. Then a two-minute performance. Nobody is judged and there is no winner.' WHERE week_number = 35;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Missing Piece — Each child is given one puzzle piece or one job (holder, counter, cheerer, fetcher). The task can only be completed if everyone does their bit. Then one job is removed and they try again.' WHERE week_number = 36;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Ten Buttons — Every child gets ten buttons. Around the hall are stations: things you need (water, food), things you want (toy, treat), and a giving jar. They spend their ten and then talk about it.' WHERE week_number = 37;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Hive — The room has to move a pile of beanbags from one end to the other, but each child may only use one specific action (roll, pass, carry, throw, catch). Nobody can do the whole job alone.' WHERE week_number = 38;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Then and Now — Children re-run one game from earlier in the year — week 3''s freeze game works well — and notice what''s different about how they play it now.' WHERE week_number = 39;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Helping Hands Relay — A course that cannot be completed alone — one child is ''stuck'' at each station and must be helped past by the next runner. The runner who helps most is the point, not the fastest.' WHERE week_number = 40;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Teach Me That — Every child teaches one thing they can do — a clap pattern, a stretch, a knot, a joke — to two other people. Then those two teach it on. Count how far one skill travels around the hall.' WHERE week_number = 41;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Spotlight, One Step — A torch spotlight on the floor. Children step into it for as long as they want — one second is fine — and the room gives a warm cheer. Nobody has to speak. Nobody may be pushed in.' WHERE week_number = 42;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Hard Right — A simple relay with a shortcut clearly available. Nobody is watching that lane. Afterwards, hands up honestly — who took it? No consequences, just the conversation.' WHERE week_number = 43;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Knot Untie — A group holds hands in a tangle and has to untangle without letting go. Requires talking, patience and not walking off. Facilitator names the moment someone nearly gives up.' WHERE week_number = 44;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Give-Away Relay — Each child starts with five beanbags and must finish with none — but they can only give them away, never drop them. Some children end up with piles. Then everyone gives again.' WHERE week_number = 45;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Full Cup — Each child fills a cup with water to where ''enough'' feels right. Then they try to carry it across the hall. The over-fillers spill. Then they try again with less.' WHERE week_number = 46;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Sprouting Seeds — Beans planted in cotton wool at week 47, checked every week to week 52. The game is a relay to plant and water them. Nothing visible happens for days.' WHERE week_number = 47;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Ripple Tag — A calm tag where being tagged means receiving a compliment, not being out. The tagged child then goes and compliments two others. Watch how fast the whole hall is tagged.' WHERE week_number = 48;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Sand Handprints — Each child presses a handprint into a shared tray of sand or dough, then adds one word for what they want to leave behind. The tray goes on the wall.' WHERE week_number = 49;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'Ten Good Things Scavenger Hunt — Teams find ten specific good things in the hall or in each other — someone''s laugh, a good pass, a kind word, a warm coat. Not objects. Noticings.' WHERE week_number = 50;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Never-Finished Tower — Build a tower. When it gets tall, add one more block. Then one more. It falls, and you start again. The game has no end and no winner. Play until time runs out.' WHERE week_number = 51;
UPDATE public.curriculum_weeks SET kids_game = 'The Whole Year Trail — Fifty-two stations is too many — pick thirteen, one per month-ish, each with an object from that session. Children walk the trail and say one thing at any station they choose. Ends with the whole room in a circle.' WHERE week_number = 52;
